# (build 169) A replay strikes no note the driver has silenced. The title's
# theme is stopped as a new song stops the last -- $FE, PlaySoundID's
# silence (silence_all: SilenceFM's key-offs, which are the driver's and no
# track's) -- and then the chip is switched, which resets it and replays the
# shadow, as the resync after COMPUTER PLAYS's FAST does with the mirror.
# Under VOICES EXTRA (the default) that replay keys from each track's own
# record, and up to build 168 a record kept its keys down until its own track
# wrote again: the theme's held chord was struck again over the silence
# (and in COMPUTER PLAYS the street's FM4 note rang on under Rolf's house's
# music). Twelve ticks after the switch the mix must still be silent.
# docs/audio.md, "Muted, then back".
start new
sound render on
wait screen title
wait ticks 420
expect sound playing
sound play 254
wait ticks 60
expect sound silent
synth chip
wait ticks 12
expect sound silent
